@@ -8,6 +8,16 @@ package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Changed
+
+- Tool input is now validated against each tool's declared `inputSchema` before its executor runs. A call the
+  schema rejects returns a readable rejection as the tool result — naming the property path and the constraint
+  that failed, never the offending value — so the model can correct the call on its next round instead of the
+  tool receiving malformed input. Executors that hand-checked their own input now only see input the schema
+  accepts; a tool that relied on producing its own error for malformed input stops seeing that input. Schemas
+  compile when a tool is registered, so a broken schema fails at startup, and extra properties the schema does
+  not declare still pass through to the executor unmodified.
+
